{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And He buried him.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, in His glory. Rabbi Yishmael says: he buried himself. And this is one of three instances of אֶת that Rabbi Yishmael expounds thus. Like it: ״בְּיוֹם מְלֹאת יְמֵי נִזְרוֹ יָבִיא אֹתוֹ״ (Numbers 6) — he brings himself. Like it: ״וְהִשִּׂיאוּ אוֹתָם עֲוֹן אַשְׁמָה״ (Leviticus 22) — and do others make them bear [guilt]? Rather, they make themselves bear [it]." "<b>Opposite Beit Pe'or.</b> His grave was prepared there from the six days of Genesis to atone for the deed of Pe'or. And this is one of the things created during twilight on the eve of Sabbath (Avot 4; Pesachim 54)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:00.624111394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}